{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015kCLWHE1b4Mj25mWqxkcrX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-msEojo/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34e6ba80-50f3-459b-ae6d-127d10268438","uuid":"77430538-ab37-4813-93eb-deaab2af2865","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:31:55.911Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-msEojo/README.md","oldString":"- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n","newString":"- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, inside the same profile as `kimi`\n  (`sandbox/agent.sb`), with a scratch HOME and a scratch `CODEX_HOME`, so the\n  agent's shell can't read or write `~/.codex`. It needs `CODEX_API_KEY` in the\n  environment, because the real `~/.codex/auth.json` is out of reach.\n","originalFile":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":6,"newStart":17,"newLines":10,"lines":[" Lanes:"," "," - `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.","+- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, inside the same profile as `kimi`","+  (`sandbox/agent.sb`), with a scratch HOME and a scratch `CODEX_HOME`, so the","+  agent's shell can't read or write `~/.codex`. It needs `CODEX_API_KEY` in the","+  environment, because the real `~/.codex/auth.json` is out of reach."," - `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the","   macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real","   home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015kCLWHE1b4Mj25mWqxkcrX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTpMd6qqVMUyktBZK6m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CBFagQ3zKFvtwFxmtFAGEP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-msEojo/ANSWER.md","content":"# codex-sandboxed lane\n\n## What I changed\n\n- **`run.sh`**: new lane `codex-sandboxed`, implemented by `codex_sandboxed_run()`.\n  - It runs the same `codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json` command as the `codex` lane, with the same prompt and timeout.\n  - The whole codex process tree runs under `sandbox-exec -D HOME=<real home> -f sandbox/agent.sb`, the same profile the `kimi` lane uses.\n  - `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME` point at a fresh scratch directory under `/tmp/chome-*`, which is removed afterwards.\n  - Codex writes its last message (`-o`) into that scratch directory, because the sandbox would block a write into the real home if the run folder were under it. The file is moved to `runs/<task>-codex-sandboxed-r<rep>/final.txt` after the sandbox exits.\n  - The header comment and the `case` dispatch list the new lane.\n- **`README.md`**: one bullet describing the lane.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`**: unchanged. Codex is installed under `/opt/homebrew`, outside the home folder, so the profile needs nothing new. It opens no part of `~/.codex`, on purpose.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n- **Sandbox probe**, run through `sandbox-exec` with the real profile:\n  - reading `~/.gitconfig` is denied;\n  - creating a file in the real home is denied;\n  - writing to the scratch HOME and to `/tmp` is allowed.\n- **Lane plumbing**: I ran `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` with a stub `codex` first on PATH. The stub recorded `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME` pointing at the scratch dir, failed to read the real `~/.gitconfig`, and wrote the `-o` file. `final.txt`, `agent.log`, `agent.err` and `meta.json` all landed in the run folder, and `check_answer.py` read the answer. The stub, the probe directories and the test run folder were deleted afterwards.\n\n## Not verified / caveats\n\n- **No real Codex run.** A real run sends the task to OpenAI, and you asked me not to submit anything to external services. The lane has not been exercised against the real `codex` binary.\n- **Authentication is the main risk.** On this machine `CODEX_API_KEY` is not set, and Codex logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`. The sandbox blocks that file, so **the lane will fail to authenticate unless `CODEX_API_KEY` is exported** when `run.sh` is called. This also means the README's older claim, that Codex \"needs nothing from the home folder\", holds only with an API key. I did not try to pass the auth file in, because the agent's shell would then be able to read it.\n- **Config is not carried over.** `CODEX_HOME` is empty, so `~/.codex/config.toml` (MCP servers, project trust levels) does not apply inside the sandboxed lane. I found no top-level `model` setting there, so the default model should match, but the run is not byte-for-byte the `codex` lane.\n- **Leftover directories I did not create.** `/tmp` contains `chome-K5ToQJ`, `chome-TURZsd` and `chome-UT8cZY`, dated earlier today. I left them alone.\n- **Nothing committed.** Changes are in the working tree only.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":683,"cache_read_input_tokens":45276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":683},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34e6ba80-50f3-459b-ae6d-127d10268438","uuid":"96db6438-f79d-4b72-9d17-9bcf58a6e778","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:32:01.002Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTpMSgiGL7hY8dcK32d","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CB