{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTqQosojkQ5LFmkR4Jo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same Codex command as the `codex` lane, with the whole Codex process tree under `sandbox/agent.sb` and a scratch HOME. I checked the sandbox and the lane plumbing, but I did not run a real Codex job, because that would send the task to OpenAI.\n\n**The catch:** on this machine `CODEX_API_KEY` is not set, and Codex logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`. The sandbox blocks that file, so **the lane will fail to authenticate unless you export `CODEX_API_KEY` before calling `run.sh`**. The README said Codex needs nothing from the home folder, which is only true with an API key. I did not pass the auth file in, because the agent's shell could then read it.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **`run.sh`**: new `codex_sandboxed_run()` and a `codex-sandboxed` case. It sets `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME` to a fresh `/tmp/chome-*` directory, runs `sandbox-exec` with `sandbox/agent.sb`, and removes the scratch directory afterwards. Codex writes its `-o` file into the scratch directory and it is moved to `final.txt` after the sandbox exits. Writing into the run folder from inside the sandbox would fail if the repo ever lives under the real home, as the README says it does on the eval Mac.\n- **`README.md`**: a bullet for the new lane.\n- **`ANSWER.md`**: what I did, what I verified, and the caveats.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`**: unchanged.\n\nHow I checked it:\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n- Under the real profile, reading `~/.gitconfig` and writing into the real home are denied. Writing to the scratch HOME and to `/tmp` is allowed.\n- I ran `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` with a stub `codex` first on PATH. The stub saw the scratch HOME and CODEX_HOME, could not read the real gitconfig, and the output landed in the run folder. I then deleted the stub and the test run folder.\n\nCaveats:\n- `~/.codex/config.toml` does not apply inside the sandboxed lane, because CODEX_HOME is empty. I found no top-level `model` setting, so the default model should match, but the run is not identical to the `codex` lane.\n- `/tmp` has three `chome-*` directories from earlier today that I did not create. I left them alone.\n- Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":233,"cache_read_input_tokens":49530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":233},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34e6ba80-50f3-459b-ae6d-127d10268438","uuid":"0a920137-11de-40ea-91ec-f46156a8f439","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:32:09.403Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTqQdU2nUzFSn5mLExW"}
